{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1773943303,"nonce":"MXTr7fd56sDspfmakeRvUyP99b8=","title":"P3: Branch selector UI + unified message action bar","message":"Add branch selector component and unified hover action bar for messages.\n\nParent: 86b63bc\n\n## Branch Selector\n- BranchSelector component: renders between a user message and divergent assistant responses at fork points\n- Design: horizontal separator bar, monospace 11px\n  - \"Branch N of M ◂ ▸\" right-aligned\n  - opacity: 0 when M=1 (invisible, zero height); 0.5 at rest when M\u003e1; 1.0 on hover\n  - ◂ ▸ arrows cycle siblings, highlight var(--accent-blue) on hover\n- Click the \"Branch N of M\" label to expand a branch overview strip:\n  - Compact cards for each branch: first ~40 chars of assistant opening text, turn count, duration\n  - Current branch has 2px left border in var(--accent-blue)\n  - Active/live branch gets pulsing dot (reuse stream-live-indicator__dot)\n  - Cards: var(--bg-card) background, border-radius: 6px, max-width ~200px, horizontal flex with overflow-x: auto\n\n## Unified Message Action Bar\n- Each message (both in History transcript-turn and Console stream-turn) gets a hover-revealed action container\n- Contains: branch selector (when applicable at this message), copy, resume-from-here, fork-from-here\n- Position: absolutely positioned so it does not affect page geometry/whitespace on show/hide\n- Appears on hover of the message container\n- Consistent between History and Console views — same component used in both\n- Dark theme: var(--bg-inset) background, subtle border, small icon buttons with tooltips\n- Icons should be minimal text/unicode, not heavy SVGs: 📋 or simple unicode for copy, ↩ for resume, ⑂ for fork\n\n## Integration\n- In History: add to ConversationDetail transcript renderer (conversations.tsx)\n- In Console: add to StreamRenderer message groups (MessageGroup.tsx or stream-turn wrapper)\n- The branch selector data (fork points, sibling counts) comes from a prop/context — the parent component provides it\n- For now, the branch selector can accept mock/empty data and render nothing when no forks exist\n- Wire to real data when P2 API is ready\n\n## CSS\n- New classes in style.css: .branch-selector, .branch-selector--active, .branch-overview, .branch-card, .message-actions\n- .message-actions: position: absolute, top: 0, right: 0 (or bottom of message), opacity: 0 on rest, opacity: 1 on parent:hover, transition 0.15s","files":null}]}